# Docs lifecycle (law)

Read skill **forja-docs-rfc-issues** when creating/editing RFCs, issues, migration docs, or feature user guides.

| Law | |
|-----|--|
| Filename status tag must match `**Status:**` | Same turn: rename + body + README + cross-links |
| Same turn as code | Flip task rows, glance Progress, indexes; feature guides if user-visible |
| Never touch `docs/backlog/` | Unless user explicitly asks |
| No ship semver in RFC/issue bodies | No `**Target version:**` / backlog links |
| Task tables append-only | Never delete/rewrite ✅/🔄 rows; new work → new IDs |
| Substantial untracked work | File RFC/issue first (or same turn as start) |

Changelog bullets → skill **forja-changelog**. Honesty / workarounds → [honesty-and-completion.mdc](./honesty-and-completion.mdc).
